@startuml component-event-service
!include <C4/C4_Component>

title ConnectSphere — Component Diagram: Event Service (C4 Level 3)
' Built so far: event status management (SCRUM-6 view as coordinator, SCRUM-7 view as organiser,
' SCRUM-8 edit status), event review and approval (SCRUM-22 to 28, 44, 45), coordinator assignment
' history (SCRUM-43), the attendee's List of events (SCRUM-71), attendee registration (SCRUM-83), the
' organiser's change requests (SCRUM-66) and the Event Coordinator Lead's queue, coordinator overview, assignment and
' reassignment (SCRUM-75, 77, 78, 79, 81; these replaced coordinator self-assignment, SCRUM-41/42), and the Safety Officer's
' Operational Safety Check (SCRUM-99, SCRUM-100) and its Home (SCRUM-165), cancelling an event (SCRUM-174), creating and
' submitting an event request (SCRUM-49) with supporting documents (SCRUM-51), drafts (SCRUM-53 to 56), withdrawing a
' registration (SCRUM-73), the registrations overview (SCRUM-74), the Lead's queue figures (SCRUM-126) and registration
' settings while an event is re-planned (SCRUM-185/AC4).
' Notifications are not sent from here: triggers write them with the change (ADR 0002), and notification-service serves them.

Container(web, "Web App", "Next.js, React", "New event request and resumed drafts, with supporting documents (/events/new, /events/new?draft=); My event requests (/my-event-requests); Registrations overview (/registrations-overview, SCRUM-74); Review queue (/events/review); event page (/events/[id]): request details, start review, approve/reject, coordinator + assignment history, status change; attendee dashboard List of events (/dashboard/attendee); Event Organiser Home, My events (/dashboard/event_organiser, SCRUM-159); registration form (/events/[id]/register), My registrations (/registrations), an event's registrations (/events/[id]/registrations); Lead pages: unassigned queue (/lead/queue), all active events with filters (/lead/events, SCRUM-189), coordinator overview (/lead/coordinators, /lead/coordinators/[id]), assign and reassign (/lead/events/[id]/assign, /reassign); Safety Officer pages: Home (/dashboard/safety_officer: figures, events waiting for a check with re-checks marked, recent decisions; SCRUM-165), events waiting for a safety check (/safety-checks), review and decide (/safety-checks/[id]), again after changes are made or an approval stops applying (SCRUM-100); the event page's Safety check section shows the coordinator and organiser every safety decision (SCRUM-100)")
System_Ext(supabaseAuth, "Supabase Auth", "Identity provider")
ContainerDb(db, "Supabase Postgres", "Postgres + RLS", "events (drafts too), event_request_attachments (SCRUM-51), users, event_change_history (SCRUM-111), event_status_history, event_comments, event_comment_mentions, event_comment_attachments, coordinator_assignment_logs, event_change_requests, event_registrations (RLS: own rows, the event's organiser and assigned coordinator); change_event_status() (a cancellation needs a reason, SCRUM-174), assign_coordinator() and list_public_events() functions; on cancel, triggers release the event's venue bookings, equipment requests and on-site assignments, close its pending change requests (also on completed) and notify the organiser and active attendees, and a cancelled event stays cancelled (SCRUM-174, migrations 60 to 63; the notification is SCRUM-172's migration 65); Lead functions lead_unassigned_queue(), lead_coordinator_overview(), lead_coordinator_events(), lead_assign_coordinator(), lead_reassign_coordinator(); events_assignment_guard trigger (only a Lead changes the coordinator; closed events never); safety_checks (SCRUM-99, read and written only through safety_check_queue(), safety_check_details(), record_safety_decision(), safety_officer_home() (the Home in one read: ready events with a re-check flag, counts, latest decisions; SCRUM-165, migration 75) and, for the event's organiser and coordinator, event_safety_decisions() (SCRUM-100)); events_safety_gate trigger (no one moves an event to confirmed until it is Safety Approved); trg_events_revoke_safety_approval trigger (an important change revokes the approval, SCRUM-100); start_safety_check_when_arranged() triggers on venue_bookings and equipment_reservations (the last approval moves a Planning event to awaiting_arrangements, SCRUM-171)")
Container(storage, "Supabase Storage", "event-attachments bucket", "Comment attachment files and event request supporting documents")
Container(notificationSvc, "Notification Service", "Node.js/TypeScript", "Serves the notification rows that this service's changes cause to be written")

Container_Boundary(eventSvc, "Event Service") {
  Component(app, "App", "Express (app.ts, server.ts)", "JSON body parsing; CORS for the web app's origin (middlewares/cors.ts); mounts /events, /lead, /safety-checks (and GET /events/:id/safety-decisions, SCRUM-100) and /change-requests. The fixed /events paths (upcoming, my-requests, my-registrations, managed, drafts) are mounted before /events/:id")
  Component(session, "Session Middleware", "middlewares/session.ts", "Reads the cs_session cookie and asks Supabase Auth who the caller is (authentication only)")
  Component(eventRoutes, "Event Status Routes", "routes/events.ts", "GET /events/:id — coordinators: any event; organisers: only events they submitted; others 403. Returns canChangeStatus / canReview for the page. PATCH /events/:id/status — assigned coordinator only (also Start review); a reason is required to reject or cancel (SCRUM-47, SCRUM-174); 409 when events_safety_gate refuses confirmed before a safety approval (SCRUM-99), or when a cancelled event would change status or a completed or rejected one be cancelled (CS174, SCRUM-174)")
  Component(reviewRoutes, "Review & Approval Routes", "routes/events.ts", "GET /events (review queue: search, status and date filters, own + unassigned), GET /events/my-events, POST /events/:id/approve, POST /events/:id/reject (reason required) — assigned coordinator only, Submitted / Under review only. GET /events/:id/outcome — latest approve/reject with reason, time and decider; none while awaiting a decision (SCRUM-44)")
  Component(commentRoutes, "Comment Routes", "routes/events.ts", "GET/POST /events/:id/comments (threaded replies, mentions, attachments), GET /events/:id/mentionable-users (coordinators + the event's organiser), POST /events/:id/attachments/upload-url (type/size checked, SCRUM-28), GET /events/:id/attachments/signed-url")
  Component(assignRoutes, "Coordinator Assignment Routes", "routes/events.ts", "GET /events/:id/assignment-history (with names). GET /events/:id/eligible-coordinators and POST /events/:id/assign-coordinator now only refuse (403): a Lead assigns and reassigns (SCRUM-78/79)")
  Component(leadMw, "Lead Middleware", "middlewares/lead.ts", "requireLead: refuses every role but event_coordinator_lead (403) before a Lead route runs (SCRUM-75)")
  Component(leadRoutes, "Lead Routes", "routes/lead.ts", "GET /lead/queue (SCRUM-77), GET /lead/summary (the figures beside the queue: events this month, the next event, reassignments this week; lead_queue_summary(), SCRUM-126), GET /lead/coordinators and /lead/coordinators/:id/events (SCRUM-81), GET /lead/events (every active event with its coordinator; RLS decides the rows, SCRUM-189), GET /lead/events/:id/assignment + POST /assign (SCRUM-78), GET /lead/events/:id/reassignment + POST /reassign (SCRUM-79). The database functions decide and enforce; the routes map their refusals to messages")
  Component(safetyMw, "Safety Officer Middleware", "middlewares/safetyOfficer.ts", "requireSafetyOfficer: refuses every role but safety_officer (403) before a safety check route runs (SCRUM-99)")
  Component(safetyRoutes, "Safety Check Routes", "routes/safetyChecks.ts", "SCRUM-99: GET /safety-checks (events ready for a check), SCRUM-165: GET /safety-checks/home (the Safety Officer Home; before /:id so 'home' is not an id), GET /safety-checks/:id (safety information and decisions), POST /safety-checks/:id/decision (Approve, Reject or Request Changes; validated with safetyDecisionProblem; Reject and Request Changes return the event to Planning, SCRUM-100, SCRUM-171). SCRUM-100: GET /events/:id/safety-decisions (every decision, for the event's coordinator and organiser). The database functions decide and enforce; the routes map their refusals to messages")
  Component(changeRoutes, "Change Request Routes", "routes/changeRequests.ts", "POST /events/:id/change-requests — organiser of the event only; validates with the shared parser, refuses draft/cancelled/rejected/completed (409), no-change requests (422) and one that changes what a pending request already changes (409 CONFLICTING_REQUEST, SCRUM-176; migration 67 checks again), inserts a pending request and never updates the event. GET /events/:id/change-requests — requests with their status")
  Component(detailsRoutes, "Event Details Routes", "routes/eventDetails.ts", "SCRUM-111: GET /events/:id/edit-form and PATCH /events/:id for the event's assigned coordinator (not for a completed, cancelled or rejected event); GET /events/:id/change-history for its coordinator and organiser. Validates with parseEventDetailsInput; saves through update_event_details() (migration 34), which updates the event and writes event_change_history together. SCRUM-112: an important change that affects the event's venue bookings or equipment requests (services/arrangementImpact.ts reads them and runs affectedArrangements from packages/shared; the change request review reuses it) answers 409 CONFIRM_IMPACT with the list, and is saved only when sent again with confirmImpact: true. SCRUM-113: that save passes the same arrangements as p_send_back, so update_event_details() (migration 40) sends them back for review in the same step")
  Component(changeReviewRoutes, "Change Request Review Routes", "routes/changeRequestReview.ts", "SCRUM-67: GET /change-requests/:id (each requested change with the current value, and what approving affects), POST /change-requests/:id/approve and /reject, for the event's assigned coordinator only. Reads the request with readChangeRequest; review_change_request() (migration 42) applies an approval through update_event_details() in the same transaction, or rejects with a reason")
  Component(upcomingRoutes, "Upcoming Events Route", "routes/upcomingEvents.ts", "GET /events/upcoming — any signed-in user; mounted before the /events/:id routes; 500 (not []) when the data cannot be loaded")
Component(myRequestRoutes, "My Event Requests Routes", "routes/myEventRequests.ts", "SCRUM-52: GET /events/my-requests (the organiser's own requests). SCRUM-159: GET /events/my-requests/home, the Event Organiser Home (My events) in one read: every own event with its coordinator, approved venues, an open clarification request and the outcome of its latest decided change request; 403 for anyone who is not an organiser. Mounted before the /events/:id routes")
  Component(upcomingRules, "Upcoming Events Rules", "services/upcomingEvents.ts", "Hides started events, sorts soonest first, picks one label (cancelled > full > closed) and maps the caller's active registration")
  Component(registrationRoutes, "Registration Routes", "routes/registrations.ts", "GET /events/:id/registration-form, POST /events/:id/registrations (Confirmed up to capacity, then Pending; 409 when closed, cancelled or already registered), POST /events/:id/registrations/:registrationId/decision (organiser confirms or declines; SCRUM-169), POST /events/:id/vip-registrations (organiser adds a VIP up to venue capacity; SCRUM-170), GET /events/my-registrations, POST /events/my-registrations/:id/withdraw (the attendee's own active registration only; anyone else's is not found; SCRUM-73), GET /events/managed (an organiser's own or a coordinator's assigned events, SCRUM-74), GET /events/:id/registrations; mounted before the /events/:id routes")
  Component(registrationRules, "Registration Rules", "services/registrations.ts", "Why a registration is refused (reuses the List of events labels and active-registration rule); maps statuses to Pending/Confirmed/Rejected/Withdrawn")
  Component(shared, "Shared Rules", "@spm-t5/shared", "isRole, canReviewEvents, isLead, EVENT_STATUSES, CLOSED_EVENT_STATUSES / isClosedEventStatus / isEventStatus, canDecideEvent, canStartReview, registrationFormSchema — same rules the web app uses")
  Component(supabaseDeps, "Supabase Client", "supabase.ts", "Publishable key + caller's token, so every query runs as the user (RLS applies)")

  Component(requestRoutes, "Event Request Routes", "routes/eventRequests.ts", "SCRUM-49: POST /events, event organisers only (403 otherwise); every bad field listed at once (422) by the shared parseEventRequest; saved through create_event_request(), which takes no organiser or organisation argument. SCRUM-123: GET /events/request-options (the room layouts the form offers)")
  Component(draftRoutes, "Draft Routes", "routes/eventDrafts.ts, routes/eventDraftDelete.ts", "SCRUM-53: POST /events/drafts (organisers only; parseEventRequestDraft lets fields be empty) via create_event_draft() (migration 70). SCRUM-54: GET and PUT /events/drafts/:id, the caller's own draft only (RLS), via update_event_draft() (migrations 71, 72); POST /events/drafts/:id/submit checks the stored draft with parseEventRequest, then submit_event_draft(); a submitted request leaves the draft flow. SCRUM-56: DELETE /events/drafts/:id via delete_event_draft() (migration 85), a draft only")
  Component(attachmentRoutes, "Request Attachment Routes", "routes/eventAttachments.ts", "SCRUM-51: POST /events/drafts/:id/attachments/upload-url (type and 10 MB size checked first), POST /events/drafts/:id/attachments, DELETE /events/drafts/:id/attachments/:attachmentId, GET /events/:id/request-attachments. Saved through add_event_attachment() and remove_event_attachment() (security definer, migration 86: the organiser's own draft only); files live under the event's folder in the event-attachments bucket")
  Component(settingsRoutes, "Registration Settings Routes", "routes/registrationSettings.ts", "SCRUM-185/AC4: GET and PUT /events/:id/registration-settings for the event's assigned coordinator: capacity (not below the Confirmed registrations) and the registration window, validated by the shared parseRegistrationSettings")
}

Rel(web, app, "Views / changes event status, reviews requests, comments, assigns coordinators (browser + server-side)", "HTTPS/JSON, session cookie")
Rel(app, detailsRoutes, "Routes event detail edits")
Rel(app, changeReviewRoutes, "Routes /change-requests")
Rel(changeReviewRoutes, db, "review_change_request() (security definer, migration 42); reads the request, the event and its arrangements", "PostgREST")
Rel(detailsRoutes, db, "update_event_details() (security definer, migration 34); reads event_change_history; reads the event's venue_bookings and equipment_reservations (SCRUM-112); sends them back for review (SCRUM-113)", "PostgREST")
Rel(app, eventRoutes, "Routes /events requests")
Rel(app, reviewRoutes, "Routes /events requests")
Rel(app, commentRoutes, "Routes /events requests")
Rel(app, assignRoutes, "Routes /events requests")
Rel(app, leadRoutes, "Routes /lead requests")
Rel(web, leadRoutes, "Lead pages load the queue, overview and assign/reassign steps; the browser confirms assignments", "HTTPS/JSON, session cookie")
Rel(leadRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(leadRoutes, leadMw, "Requires an Event Coordinator Lead")
Rel(leadRoutes, shared, "Checks isClosedEventStatus for the assign/reassign action")
Rel(leadRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Calls the lead_* functions (security invoker reads; security definer assign/reassign with the Lead check inside); reads events as the Lead (RLS)")
Rel(app, safetyRoutes, "Routes /safety-checks requests")
Rel(web, safetyRoutes, "Safety Officer pages load the Home, the queue and an event's safety information; the browser submits the decision", "HTTPS/JSON, session cookie")
Rel(safetyRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(safetyRoutes, safetyMw, "Requires a Safety Officer")
Rel(safetyRoutes, shared, "Runs safetyDecisionProblem and SAFETY_DECISION_LABELS (same rules as the web form)")
Rel(safetyRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Calls safety_check_queue(), safety_officer_home(), safety_check_details() and record_safety_decision() (security definer, each checks the caller is a Safety Officer)")
Rel(app, changeRoutes, "Routes /events/:id/change-requests")
Rel(app, upcomingRoutes, "Routes /events/upcoming")
Rel(app, myRequestRoutes, "Routes /events/my-requests")
Rel(app, registrationRoutes, "Routes registration requests")
Rel(changeRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(changeRoutes, shared, "Checks canRequestChange and runs parseEventChangeRequestInput (same rules as the web form)")
Rel(changeRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Reads the event; inserts into event_change_requests (RLS: own event, allowed status, pending)")
Rel(eventRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(reviewRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(commentRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(assignRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(upcomingRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(myRequestRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(upcomingRoutes, upcomingRules, "Turns rows into the List of events")
Rel(registrationRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(registrationRoutes, registrationRules, "Checks the event is open and the attendee has no active registration")
Rel(registrationRules, upcomingRules, "Reuses canRegister() and myRegistration()")
Rel(registrationRoutes, shared, "Validates name, email and contact number")
Rel(registrationRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Calls list_public_events(), register_for_event(), decide_registration(), add_vip_registration(), my_contact_details() (the form's prefill) and event_registration_contacts(); reads and withdraws event_registrations (migration 29: an attendee may only set their own active row to withdrawn)")
Rel(session, supabaseAuth, "Verifies session token", "HTTPS")
Rel(eventRoutes, shared, "Checks role and status values")
Rel(reviewRoutes, shared, "Checks canReviewEvents and canDecideEvent")
Rel(assignRoutes, shared, "Checks roles")
Rel(commentRoutes, shared, "Checks roles and attachment type/size (same rules as the web app)")
Rel(eventRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Queries events and users; calls change_event_status()")
Rel(reviewRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Queries events and users; calls change_event_status() to approve/reject; reads event_status_history for the outcome")
Rel(commentRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Reads/writes comments, mentions, attachments; creates signed URLs")
Rel(assignRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Reads coordinator_assignment_logs, users and the event")
Rel(upcomingRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Calls list_public_events() (security definer: supplies each public event's venue, Confirmed registration count and the caller's own active registration)")
Rel(myRequestRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Calls organiser_home() (security definer, migration 76: the organiser's own events with their coordinator, approved venues, an unanswered clarification request and the latest decided change request)")
Rel(supabaseDeps, db, "Reads; status change + history and assignment + log each written in one transaction", "PostgREST / RPC")
Rel(supabaseDeps, storage, "Creates signed upload and download URLs for attachments", "HTTPS")
Rel(web, storage, "Uploads attachment files to the signed upload URL; opens them via signed download URLs", "HTTPS")

Rel(app, requestRoutes, "Routes POST /events and /events/request-options")
Rel(requestRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(requestRoutes, shared, "parseEventRequest (same rules as the web form)")
Rel(requestRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Reads the caller's role and room_layouts; calls create_event_request()")
Rel(app, draftRoutes, "Routes /events/drafts")
Rel(draftRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(draftRoutes, shared, "parseEventRequestDraft to save, parseEventRequest to submit")
Rel(draftRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Reads the caller's own draft (RLS); calls create_event_draft(), update_event_draft(), submit_event_draft() and delete_event_draft()")
Rel(app, attachmentRoutes, "Routes draft attachments and /events/:id/request-attachments")
Rel(attachmentRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(attachmentRoutes, shared, "canCreateEventRequests; attachmentRefusal (accepted types, 10 MB)")
Rel(attachmentRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Calls add_event_attachment() and remove_event_attachment(); reads event_request_attachments; creates signed upload URLs and removes files")
Rel(app, settingsRoutes, "Routes /events/:id/registration-settings")
Rel(settingsRoutes, session, "Requires a signed-in caller")
Rel(settingsRoutes, shared, "parseRegistrationSettings validates the capacity and window")
Rel(settingsRoutes, supabaseDeps, "Reads the event and its Confirmed registration count; update_registration_settings() (migration 84) saves them, only for the assigned coordinator, and logs each change")
Rel(db, notificationSvc, "Triggers write notification rows in the same transaction as the change they announce (ADR 0002; migrations 44, 65, 69, 82, 83)", "Shared database")

@enduml
